 ## Native prompt overlay successor
 
 This successor uses only the frozen UIv3 prompt overlay product. The observer follows the actual delayed DrawPromptWindow callback and retains every prior real input/command/physical assertion. Review actual screenshots: the human Italian edge prompt and robot source-selection cancellation line must remain readable over lower native HUD/gizmo rows. Viewport geometry alone does not establish rendering acceptance. No new backend or provider scope.
+
+
+## Native prompt overlay successor
+
+This successor uses only the frozen UIv4 prompt overlay product. The observer follows the actual delayed DrawPromptWindow callback and retains every prior real input/command/physical assertion. Review actual screenshots: the human Italian edge prompt and robot source-selection cancellation line must remain readable over lower native HUD/gizmo rows. Viewport geometry alone does not establish rendering acceptance. No new backend or provider scope. The human worker separately moves to the real option before posting Shift-down, then holds that key through the mouse event and releases it in finally after a bounded native option observation. This is unproven input delivery until actual QueueOrder=true is observed; no event modifier, key-binding or UI state is assigned.
